Question Title: Execute a Python Script Directly

Question Link:
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/mepmefz373b4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg

Solution:
echo "#!/usr/bin/env python3" > hello.py
echo "print('Hello from Python')" >> hello.py
chmod 777 hello.py
./hello.py

Approach:
1. write the shebang to tell the computer which compiler or interpretor to use for the given code
2. write the program to be executed
3. give the file execution permission

Result:
python file executes directly from terminal